==Battleground==
*20 [[Those Guys]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*2 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Doge]] spawns after 11.33 seconds<sup>340f</sup>.
*1 [[Relic Doge]] spawns after 44.67 seconds<sup>1,340f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 168.67 seconds<sup>5,060f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Le'mammoth]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**2 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
**5 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**2 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Aku Shield Piercers are unnecessary. You should bring [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], 1-2 meatshields, and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]. The Relics may seem intimidating, but once you've built up a stack of Couriers and Can Cans, both the Sir Rels and the Relic Doges will be a cakewalk to deal with.

Deploy a meatshield and both Can Can and Courier at the start. Send out Ururun and a [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]], then the stage should become trivial from there.

